-- title:
--   Local character comparison for factors of a p-power norm
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by a prime number $p$, let $E=A[X]/(\Phi_p(X))$ with root $\zeta$ and $\pi=\zeta-1$, and let $\varepsilon$ be augmentation. If $F,K\in A[\mathbb Z/p^{e+1}]$ and a unit $b$ satisfy
--   $$
--   FK=p^{e+1}\,b,
--   $$
--   then $F(\zeta)=w\,\varepsilon(F)$ for a unit $w$ of $E$ with $w-1\in(\pi)$, and likewise for $K$.
--
--   The value of each factor at an order-$p$ character equals its augmentation up to a unit congruent to $1$ modulo $\zeta-1$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/LinearAlgebra/CirculantHadamard/LocalComparison.lean#L79-L141

